    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d43">

                <pb facs="0055" n="43" sameAs="frus:frus1942v05/pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">710.Consultatlon 3/552: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-31T12:00:00-04:00">January 31,
                        1942—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received 7:40 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>186. Saw Rossetti last night in company with Mendez, Vice President, and the
                    Minister said he will present resolutions of Rio to Congress next week and go
                    before that body to insist on speedy ratification. He is confident he will
                    succeed. This is undoubtedly the program since Mendez has instructed along this
                    line. Rossetti said we may be sure that within a month the Axis Missions will
                    have departed.<anchor n="79" xml:id="d43-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d43-f1" n="79" xml:id="d43-f1-content">
                <p>For correspondence on the Chilean breach with the Axis, see <ref
                        target="frus1942v06">vol. <hi rendition="#small-caps">vi</hi></ref>, section
                    under Chile entitled “Efforts to secure cooperation between the United States
                    and Chile on certain measures for Hemisphere defense.”</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
